<title>USA: White House doubts Fed nominations this week.</title>
<headline>White House doubts Fed nominations this week.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House spokesman Mike McCurry said on Monday he doubted there would be announcements this week on filling the two Federal Reserve Board vacancies.</p>
<p>After saying earlier on Monday that the White House was &quot;close&quot; to an announcement, McCurry was asked at his midday briefing if he expected one on Monday and replied: &quot;I don't expect it today, no. In fact, I doubt it will be this week.&quot;</p>
<p>Earlier on Monday, National Economic Council Chairman Gene Sperling also said the White House was &quot;close&quot; to wrapping the matter up but gave no further details.</p>
